  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q35-group-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following, expressing roots as fractional exponents.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p4-q35-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x\\sqrt{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^{\\frac32}$, $x\\ge0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x\\sqrt{x}&=x\\times x^{\\frac12}\\\\x\\sqrt{x}&=x^{1+\\frac12}\\\\x\\sqrt{x}&=x^{\\frac32}\\end{align*}$$The original square root requires $x\\ge0$ over the reals.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q36-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2\\sqrt[3]{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^{\\frac73}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2\\sqrt[3]{x}&=x^2\\times x^{\\frac13}\\\\x^2\\sqrt[3]{x}&=x^{2+\\frac13}\\\\x^2\\sqrt[3]{x}&=x^{\\frac73}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q37-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt[3]{8y^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2y^{\\frac23}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt[3]{8y^2}&=8^{\\frac13}y^{\\frac23}\\\\\\sqrt[3]{8y^2}&=2y^{\\frac23}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q38-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt{9y^3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3y^{\\frac32}$, $y\\ge0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{9y^3}&=9^{\\frac12}y^{\\frac32}\\\\\\sqrt{9y^3}&=3y^{\\frac32}\\end{align*}$$For a real square root, $9y^3\\ge0$, so $y\\ge0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
  },
